<% page_title "Terms" %>

<article class="wrap measure">
  <h1 class="text-4xl">Terms of service</h1>

  <div class="mt-10 space-y-8 text-ink-600">
    <section>
      <h2 class="text-2xl text-ink-950">The service</h2>
      <p class="mt-2">
        AI Pop Music licenses generated songs to subscribers. The <%= link_to "license page", page_license_path, class: "underline" %>
        forms part of these terms.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section>
      <h2 class="text-2xl text-ink-950">Accounts</h2>
      <p class="mt-2">
        One account per person or organisation. You are responsible for keeping your
        credentials private; downloads are recorded against your account.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section>
      <h2 class="text-2xl text-ink-950">Billing</h2>
      <p class="mt-2">
        Plans are billed monthly in advance. A plan covers the number of genres stated on it.
        Changing genres does not change the price. Cancelling stops future downloads
        immediately; completed periods are not refunded.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section>
      <h2 class="text-2xl text-ink-950">Availability and changes</h2>
      <p class="mt-2">
        Tracks may be retired from the catalogue, but a retired track stays licensed for work
        you already published. We will not withdraw the rights granted for downloads you hold.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section>
      <h2 class="text-2xl text-ink-950">Acceptable use</h2>
      <p class="mt-2">
        Do not use the catalogue unlawfully, do not attempt to extract the catalogue in bulk,
        and do not resell tracks as music. Accounts doing so are closed.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section>
      <h2 class="text-2xl text-ink-950">Liability</h2>
      <p class="mt-2">
        Tracks are provided as-is. Our liability is limited to the amount you paid in the twelve
        months before a claim. Nothing here limits rights you have under consumer law.
      </p>
    </section>
  </div>
</article>
